node_modules
.next
out
.git
.github

# The sidecar is a separate image built from ./enquiry with its own
# Dockerfile, so the site build has never needed this directory — it was just
# being copied in and ignored. It stopped being harmless when the invoice
# builder added .woff2 files under enquiry/fonts: the Turbopack build began
# failing to resolve next/font's own google-font shim, twenty times over, on
# the commit that added them and on every commit after. Nothing in src/
# changed and the same build passes locally, cold and with NODE_ENV=production.
#
# The mechanism is not proven. Keeping the directory out of the context is
# right on its own terms, and it is the only variable that changed.
enquiry/

# Reference capture — hundreds of MB, not needed to build
capture/
design/
docs/
deliverables/
brand/*.png

*.md
!README.md
.DS_Store

# Image derivatives live in GCS behind the CDN, not in the container. The
# build only needs src/generated/images.json — it reads dimensions, LQIPs and
# the derivative paths from the manifest and emits absolute CDN URLs, so
# shipping the files too would add ~165 MB to every push and node pull for
# bytes nginx would never serve.
#
# Keep public/brand: the logo SVGs are tiny and are referenced same-origin.
public/img/
